## The DRY line

This file is the standing statement on **making a measurement comparable**, which includes holding the code constant rather than its label. It composes with [`filing-defects-across-repos`](filing-defects-across-repos.mdc) (whose step 7 applies the revision-citing half to a report crossing a repository boundary, and points here for the evidence) and with [`long-running-commands`](long-running-commands.mdc) (which owns *bounding* a run and not trampling a concurrent one; this rule owns whether the number it produces means anything). Per-suite timing facts, such as what the band costs or what the serial tail costs, belong in the issues that measured them, not here.

It also composes with the [`local-ci`](../../.claude/skills/local-ci/SKILL.md) skill, which owns the gate's own job definition and is itself a parity reference worth reading before benchmarking against CI.
